# worldprobe code.

image /tmp/probe_world.png

# ── TWO PINS RE-AIMED 2026-08-11; THE OTHER TWO ARE THE ORIGINAL JUNE ONES ──────────────
# `vis_grass` and `rem_grass` still pass at the coordinates measured 2026-06-12, at dmax=0.
# That is what says the bake formula never moved — and `rem_grass` only came back when
# src/worldprobe.loft's lost write was fixed (it bound `vv = s.vis` and mutated the COPY, so
# the scene rendered 0 remembered cells and this probe had been asserting a state the scene
# never built). `road` and `wall_untinted` moved because plan #17 cut gates in the town wall
# and posted a guard on the works: a wall now stands where the road pin was, and open ground
# where the wall pin was. ⚠ The expected colours are unchanged — only the sample positions,
# each re-aimed at the most uniform pixel of its own feature (road 13x13, wall 11x11).

probe vis_grass 400 420 165 175 114 tol 4
probe rem_grass 106 360 74 79 51 tol 4
probe road 78 465 173 156 121 tol 4
probe wall_untinted 791 273 38 36 33 tol 4
